<div id="recipe-83058-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-83058-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="83058"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Instructions</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-83058-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Place tomatoes, cucumbers, scallions, and green peppers in a large bowl or a large platter.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/shepherd-salad-recipe-Turkish-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Side by side images showing the ingredients of Turkish shepherd's salad." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/shepherd-salad-recipe-Turkish-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/shepherd-salad-recipe-Turkish-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/shepherd-salad-recipe-Turkish-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/shepherd-salad-recipe-Turkish-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/shepherd-salad-recipe-Turkish.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/shepherd-salad-recipe-Turkish.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-83058-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Drizzle it with lemon juice, olive oil, and season with salt, pepper, and sumac.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-83058-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Sprinkle it with fresh parsley and toss to combine.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Coban-salad-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Side by side photos showing the making of coban salad." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Coban-salad-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Coban-salad-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Coban-salad-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Coban-salad-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Coban-salad.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Coban-salad.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-83058-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Serve it right away.</div></li></ul></div></div>

<div id="recipe-83058-notes" class="wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Notes</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-notes"><ul>
<li><strong>Yields:&nbsp;</strong>This recipe makes about 6 cups of salad (depending on the size of your vegetables), and it is ideal for 4 (large) servings. The nutritional values below are per serving.</li>
<li><strong>Storage:&nbsp;</strong>Place leftovers in an airtight container and keep them in the fridge for up to 2 days. It is normal for the vegetables to release their juices as they sit. Just give it a stir before serving.</li>
<li><strong>Optional add-ins:&nbsp;</strong>As I was writing this recipe, I wanted to stay true to the traditional recipe. However, some modern-day versions of this recipe add other ingredients like a handful of crumbled feta cheese, chopped black olives, and a sprinkle of red pepper flakes (or Urfa chile if you can get your hands on.) All of these would be great addition to the recipe.</li>
</ul></div></div>
